  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q16-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "Let $a,b\\geq0$ and $n\\in\\mathbb{N}$. Prove that $(ab)^{1/n}=a^{1/n}b^{1/n}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(ab)^{1/n}=a^{1/n}b^{1/n}$.\n\nRaise the nonnegative product of the roots to the power $n$, then take the nonnegative $n$th root.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(a^{1/n}b^{1/n})^n&=(a^{1/n})^n(b^{1/n})^n\\\\(a^{1/n}b^{1/n})^n&=ab\\end{align*}$$\nSince $a^{1/n}b^{1/n}\\geq0$, taking the nonnegative $n$th root gives\n$$(ab)^{1/n}=a^{1/n}b^{1/n}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 45
  },
